The numerator of $\frac{\partial A_{HD}}{\partial C_A}$ becomes:

N(C_A) = C_A^{\gamma_D - 1} \left[\gamma_D (1 + \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega}) - \sigma_\Omega \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega}\right]

= C_A^{\gamma_D - 1} \left[\gamma_D + \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\gamma_D - \sigma_\Omega)\right]

Step 3: Critical Threshold

Setting $N(C_A) = 0$:

\gamma_D + \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\gamma_D - \sigma_\Omega) = 0

\eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D) = \gamma_D

Since $\sigma_\Omega > \gamma_D$ (strict inequality assumed for non-trivial threshold), we solve:

C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} = \frac{\gamma_D}{\eta_\Omega \Omega (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D)}

C_{A,\text{crit}} = \left( \frac{\gamma_D}{\eta_\Omega \Omega (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D)} \right)^{\frac{1}{\sigma_\Omega}}

Step 4: Sign Analysis

For $C_A > C_{A,\text{crit}}$:

C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} > \frac{\gamma_D}{\eta_\Omega \Omega (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D)}

\eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D) > \gamma_D

\gamma_D + \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\gamma_D - \sigma_\Omega) < 0

Since $C_A^{\gamma_D - 1} > 0$ for all $C_A > 0$, we conclude $N(C_A) < 0$, hence $\frac{\partial A_{HD}}{\partial C_A} < 0$.

For $C_A < C_{A,\text{crit}}$, the inequality reverses, giving $N(C_A) > 0$ and $\frac{\partial A_{HD}}{\partial C_A} > 0$.

Step 5: Uniqueness

The function $G(C_A) = \eta_\Omega \Omega C_A^{\sigma_\Omega} (\sigma_\Omega - \gamma_D)$ is strictly increasing in $C_A$ (since $\sigma_\Omega > 0$ and $\sigma_\Omega > \gamma_D$). Therefore, it crosses $\gamma_D$ exactly once, establishing uniqueness of $C_{A,\text{crit}}$. $\blacksquare$

