A.4 Comparative Statics of the Minimum Deliberation Bound

Proposition A.4.1 (Opacity Sensitivity). The elasticity of $\Delta t_{\min}$ with respect to opacity $\Omega$ is:

\varepsilon_{\Omega} = \frac{\partial \ln \Delta t_{\min}}{\partial \ln \Omega} = \frac{\alpha}{\beta}

Proof.

\ln \Delta t_{\min} = \frac{1}{\beta} [\alpha \ln \Omega + \gamma \ln K - \ln H_{A,\max}]

\frac{\partial \ln \Delta t_{\min}}{\partial \ln \Omega} = \frac{\alpha}{\beta}

$\square$

Implication: If $\alpha = \beta$ (opacity and latency have symmetric effects), then a doubling of model opacity ($\Omega \to 2\Omega$) requires a doubling of minimum deliberation time ($\Delta t_{\min} \to 2\Delta t_{\min}$) to maintain the Authority Auditability Condition.

Proposition A.4.2 (Complexity Sensitivity). The elasticity of $\Delta t_{\min}$ with respect to complexity $K$ is:

\varepsilon_K = \frac{\partial \ln \Delta t_{\min}}{\partial \ln K} = \frac{\gamma}{\beta}

Proof. Identical derivation as A.4.1. $\square$

Proposition A.4.3 (Audit Capacity Sensitivity). The elasticity of $\Delta t_{\min}$ with respect to maximum audit capacity $H_{A,\max}$ is:

\varepsilon_{H} = \frac{\partial \ln \Delta t_{\min}}{\partial \ln H_{A,\max}} = -\frac{1}{\beta}

Proof.

\ln \Delta t_{\min} = \frac{1}{\beta} [\alpha \ln \Omega + \gamma \ln K - \ln H_{A,\max}]

\frac{\partial \ln \Delta t_{\min}}{\partial \ln H_{A,\max}} = -\frac{1}{\beta}

$\square$

Implication: Increasing audit capacity by a factor of 2 reduces minimum deliberation time by a factor of $2^{-1/\beta}$. If $\beta = 1$, doubling audit capacity halves minimum deliberation time.

